content.text:
The evidence points to one root cause: ts-travel-plan-service's outbound POSTs to seat-service are rewritten to `/error` and fail with 403. Its own handlers then return 500, which reaches the dashboard.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "fault_kind": "http_response_body_corrupted",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind='Client') OR (service_name='ts-seat-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY n DESC",
          "claim": "Travel-plan's client POSTs to seat-service return 403 on the path 'POST /error' (239 spans), while seat's GET calls return 200."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name AS callee, c.span_name, c.attr_http_response_status_code AS code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces pa JOIN abnormal_traces c ON c.parent_span_id = pa.span_id AND c.trace_id = pa.trace_id WHERE pa.service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND pa.span_name='POST' AND pa.attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY n DESC",
          "claim": "Travel-plan's POST calls to seat-service fail with 403 and never reach the seat left_tickets path; route-plan calls return 200."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_http_response_status_code=500 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS http500, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "All travel-plan server endpoints (minStation, cheapest, quickest) return HTTP 500 during the incident."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT level, substr(message,1,160) AS m, count(*) AS c FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND level <> 'INFO' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Travel-plan logs SEVERE HttpClientErrorException Forbidden exceptions from its seat-service call, about 239 times."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_http_response_status_code>=500 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS http5xx FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('ts-ui-dashboard') AND span_name LIKE '%travelPlan%' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Dashboard's travelPlan requests return HTTP 500, matching travel-plan's failing endpoints, so users see the error."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

